/-!
# Relatively semiample invertible modules over an affine open

Let `f : Y ⟶ S` be quasi-compact and quasi-separated and let `L` be an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module
which is relatively semiample: every point of `S` has an open neighbourhood `V` such that some
positive power `L^{⊗ d}` is generated by its sections over `f⁻¹(V)`. Then over every affine open
`U ⊆ S` one positive power `L^{⊗ D}` of the restriction of `L` to `f⁻¹(U)` is generated by
finitely many global sections.

Near a point `y ∈ f⁻¹(U)`, a section over `f⁻¹(V)` nonvanishing at `y` becomes, after
multiplication by a power of a function `a` on `U` with `f(y) ∈ D(a) ⊆ V`, the restriction of a
section over `f⁻¹(U)` (the qcqs extension of sections from a basic open); quasi-compactness of
`f⁻¹(U)` leaves finitely many of them, and raising each to a power brings them to one degree.

## Main results

* `MMP.SemiampleSections.exists_covering_powSections_restrict`: finitely many global sections of
  one positive power of the restriction of `L` to `f⁻¹(U)` whose nonvanishing loci cover it.
* `MMP.SemiampleSections.exists_generatesStalks_restrict`: the same, as a family of `N + 1`
  sections generating every stalk.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PS)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

